{"version":"scxml.report/v3","kind":"validator","validator":{"source_name":"tests/ui/scxml082-names-over-name-bound.scxml","source_text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"start\">\n  <state id=\"start\">\n    <onentry>\n      <raise event=\"\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <invoke id=\"\" src=\"child.scxml\"/>\n  </state>\n</scxml>\n","diagnostics":[{"severity":"error","code":"SCXML082","category":"semantic","message":"`<raise>` event name `exxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have","primary":{"span":{"start":133,"end":1158},"message":"1,025 bytes"},"secondary":[],"notes":["every build bounds an event name to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this `<raise>` could never run as written; SCXML 1.0 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)"],"help":"shorten the `event` value to at most 1,024 bytes","spec_references":["SCXML 1.0 §4.2 <raise>"],"fixes":[]},{"severity":"error","code":"SCXML082","category":"semantic","message":"`<invoke>` ID `ixxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,013 bytes, so the `done.invoke.` event it raises is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have","primary":{"span":{"start":1193,"end":2206},"message":"`done.invoke.` and these 1,013 bytes make 1,025"},"secondary":[],"notes":["SCXML 1.0 §6.4: a finished invoked service \"MUST return a special event 'done.invoke.id' to the external event queue of the invoking process, where id is the invokeid for this invocation\"; every build bounds an event name to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this invocation could never report that it finished; SCXML 1.0 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)"],"help":"shorten the ID to at most 1,012 bytes","spec_references":["SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>"],"fixes":[]}],"counts":{"errors":2,"warnings":0,"notes":0,"total":2}}}